# and/or give one of their operands, a condition reads its truthiness (wiki/truthiness.md; decision and-or-values)
'7 and "hi"'	"hi"
'0 and 5'	0
'0 or 5'	5
'3 or 4'	3
'ø or 3'	3
'name = ""; name or "anonymous"'	"anonymous"
'[] or [1]'	[1]
'if 0 or 5 { "taken" } else { "not" }'	"taken"
'1 and 0 or 2'	2
